 ### Account and group writes

+A user id is an identifier, never proof of anything. Clients can read other users' ids in `SpaceAccess`, `ResourceAccess`, `group_membership` and `my_pseudo_accounts`, and a group's id is also a user id. So knowing an id must give no power over its user: no client write may add a user to a group, or grant them access, without that user's own action (ENG-2456).
+
 - `authenticated` can't insert into `PlatformAccount`, and has `UPDATE` on it per column, so clients can't set who owns an account (`dg_account`) or change what identifies it (`agent_type`, `platform`, `account_local_id`). A new column isn't client-writable until it's added to the grant. Clients create and upsert accounts through `upsert_account_in_space`, which also adds the account to the space (ENG-2447).
 - `upsert_account_in_space` requires editor access to the space, and grants no `SpaceAccess` (ENG-2439). `LocalAccess` says an account belongs to a space and grants nothing.
 - `LocalAccess` writes require editor access to the row's own space (ENG-2447).
-- Only a group's admins can add members. The `create-group` edge function adds the first admin with the service role, and `accept_group_invitation` adds invited members (ENG-2438).
+- Clients can't insert into `group_membership`, and can update only its `admin` column, so admins can grant and withdraw admin rights but can't turn a membership into someone else's. The `create-group` edge function adds the first admin with the service role, and `accept_group_invitation` adds invited members (ENG-2438, ENG-2456).
+- A new or updated `SpaceAccess` or `ResourceAccess` grant must go to the caller or a group the caller belongs to (ENG-2456). So an editor can't change the permissions of another user's grant, though they can still delete it.

 ### Account reads

